A second mechanism from the same commit is adapted in src/preservation-prompt.ts: the
USER_MESSAGES_SACRED_BLOCK and RELEVANT_FILES_BLOCK constants come from
conductors/compaction-naive/compaction-naive.ts:109-156 (COMPACTION_SYSTEM) -- the
"USER MESSAGES ARE SACRED" rule with its instruction to reproduce every user message
verbatim and in order, its parenthetical naming what IS summarized by contrast, the
`## Relevant files` section with a per-file reason, and the "(none)" placeholder
convention that keeps a section present when empty. Adapted rather than taken whole:
upstream's COMPACTION_SYSTEM is a complete system prompt dictating a seven-section output
shape, because upstream owns its summarization call end to end. This project does not --
pi's own SUMMARIZATION_SYSTEM_PROMPT and SUMMARIZATION_PROMPT are the system and base
prompts and customInstructions is appended to the base prompt -- so these blocks are
written as ADDITIONS to a structure pi already specified. Upstream's "no prose outside
the sections" rule and its Goal/Progress/Key decisions/Next steps/Critical context
section list are deliberately NOT taken: pi's own prompt already asks for that material
under its own headings, and dictating a competing list from customInstructions would
fight the primitive this package exists to preserve.

Nothing else from Accordion is used here -- its fidelity ladder, fold/digest engine,
Tauri GUI, WebSocket transport and `context`-hook interception are all out of scope for
a router.

